      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, what happens if caller A setEnabled(false) and caller B immediately afterwards calls setEnabled(true)? B will immediately get a callback that says the operation suceeded, but when it tries to use the controller, it will actually be disabled. That\u0027s why I think it\u0027s better to just say the app shouldn\u0027t look at the OutcomeReceiver#onResult at all, and just listen for the callbacks.",
