      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems unwise to write the persistent settings when receiving the callback that says the state changed. This is because if changing the state fails, the persistent setting is never changed, and if for whatever reason the state gets stuck, the perisstent setting cannot be changed without a reboot. It seems better for the persistent setting to described the *desired* state, and update it whenever the code tries to change the state.",
